 "unknowns": [
  "whether the Batmobile's LocalToWorld carries a non-unit Z scale: if it does, the value is scaleZ*cos(tilt) and the 0.707 thresholds would be scale-relative. The dump declares the matrix, not how the scale is folded in. Told apart by reading the lengths of the three LocalToWorld rows on a live mesh.",
  "row-versus-column reading of the element: `FMatrix` is declared as four FPlanes (XPlane/YPlane/ZPlane/WPlane), so element 10 is ZPlane.Z either way and for an orthonormal basis the two readings give the same scalar; only the axis naming (local Z vs world Z) differs and the bytes cannot separate them.",
  "which component of the angle the test means in gameplay terms (pitch-only vs pitch+roll combined) is not separable from LocalToWorld.Z.Z alone: it is the total tilt of the up axis, and splitting pitch from roll needs the other elements.",
  "why the -0.707 branch exists (the BatmobileStuckTimeFlip >= BatmobileStuckTime exemption): the two timer fields are decoded by name, but their writers/tick logic are not decoded here."
 ]
